Bundled third-party components
------------------------------

These remain licensed under their own terms. All are inlined into dist/ by
esbuild at build time; the published VSIX ships no node_modules tree and no
native binaries.

- pdf-lib — MIT License — https://github.com/Hopding/pdf-lib
- qrcode-generator — MIT License — https://github.com/kazuhikoarase/qrcode-generator
- zod — MIT License — https://github.com/colinhacks/zod
- React and ReactDOM — MIT License — https://github.com/facebook/react
- pdf.js (pdfjs-dist) — Apache License 2.0 — https://github.com/mozilla/pdf.js
- @modelcontextprotocol/sdk — MIT License — https://github.com/modelcontextprotocol/typescript-sdk

SQLite is reached through the Node.js `node:sqlite` builtin — no third-party
SQLite driver is bundled. (better-sqlite3 was removed at M7; it is no longer a
dependency of any kind, so it is no longer listed above.)

The optional local Python backend (PyMuPDF, and the system Tesseract OCR binary)
is not bundled; it is installed separately by the user and remains under its
respective licenses.

Full license texts are available at the URLs above and within each component's
distribution.
